#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c963c1-98e9-5a2d-a5c7-0f6d04dbda30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291758} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c36bc2-4930-5d0c-9a5f-14d8dcb8f959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291759} {:answer/id #uuid "590404f5-f3f8-532b-aeb2-8ac76e440df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291760} {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} {:answer/id #uuid "850318a6-1a4d-5307-b80c-b8e0f486b5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca356f0b-e266-5dae-b876-0c22bbf0bfe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95af1977-8d23-5d4e-89a9-245a921e273b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102806" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5=2x-3y \\\\ 4x=y-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
